                                        "entry_id": "f8d9fda3-b185-3898-a763-a70ca30b3e18",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The goddess of wisdom, especially strategic warfare, and the arts, especially crafts and in particular weaving. She is the Roman counterpart of Athena."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Roman"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3372b2b7-05de-4199-9fbb-4d8472c0557e",
                                                "sense_id": "c888d41e-da9b-36c3-b667-043fce601b3f",
                                                "text": "In many works of this ſpecies, the hero is allowed to be mortal, and to become wiſe and virtuous as well as happy, by a train of events and circumſtances. The heroines, on the contrary, are to be born immaculate; and to act like goddeſſes of wiſdom, juſt come forth highly finiſhed Minervas from the head of Jove."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
